  "chapter": {
    "number": 5,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "For the end, a Psalm of David, concerning her that inherits."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Listen to my words, O Lord,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 8
          },
          {
            "text": "attend to my cry.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Attend to the voice of my supplication, my King, and my God: for to you, O Lord, will I pray.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In the morning you shall hear my voice: in the morning will I wait upon you, and will look up.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you are not a god that desires iniquity; neither shall the worker of wickedness dwell with you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Neither shall the transgressors continue in your sight: you hate, O Lord, all them that work iniquity.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You will destroy all that speak falsehood: the Lord abhors the bloody and deceitful man.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I will enter into your house in the multitude of your mercy: I will worship in your fear toward your holy temple.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Lead me, O Lord, in your righteousness because of my enemies; make my way plain before your face.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For there is no truth in their mouth; their heart is vain; their throat is an open sepulchre; with their tongues they have used deceit.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Judge them, O God; let them",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 9
          },
          {
            "text": "fail of their counsels: cast them out according to the abundance of their ungodliness; for they have provoked you, O Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But let all that trust on you be glad in you: they shall exult for ever, and you shall dwell among them; and all that love your name shall rejoice in you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you, Lord, shall bless the righteous: you have",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 10
          },
          {
            "text": "compassed us as with a shield of favor.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
